ΙΧΘΥΣ

ΙΧΘΥΣ (Ichthys) is an ancient Greek acronym meaning:

ΙΗΣΟΥΣ ΧΡΙΣΤΟΣ ΘΕΟΥ ΥΙΟΣ ΣΩΤΗΡ
(Jesus Christ, Son of God, Savior)

The fish symbol (ΙΧΘΥΣ) became one of the earliest and most recognizable symbols of Christianity. During the first centuries of the Christian era, believers used the fish as a discreet sign of identification and faith, especially during periods of persecution within the Roman Empire. Over time, it became a lasting symbol of Jesus Christ and the Christian message.

This document is organized as follows:
* First line: the Bitcoin OP_RETURN transaction hash.
* Second line: the language, the corresponding national flag, and the translated phrase "Jesus Christ, Son of God, Savior".
* Each entry represents an individual inscription recorded on the Bitcoin blockchain.

